<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Billung</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">10th century–1106</span> · Also known as Billung dynasty, Billungs</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Billung was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> noble family whose members were dukes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> from the 10th century until 1106. Its founder, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hermann-billung">Hermann Billung</a>, was given command of the frontier against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavs">Slavs</a> along the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elbe">Elbe</a> by Otto I around 936, the region later called the Billung March. The line ended with Duke Magnus in 1106, and the duchy passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lothair-iii-holy-roman-emperor">Lothair of Supplinburg</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-billung.jpg" alt="House of Billung" width="320" height="441" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lucas Cranach the Younger · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hermann_Billung.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
